.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_SIGN 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_sign ,
.Nm X509_sign_ctx ,
.Nm X509_REQ_sign ,
.Nm X509_REQ_sign_ctx ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_sign ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_sign_ctx ,
.Nm X509_CRL_sign ,
.Nm X509_CRL_sign_ctx
.Nd sign certificate, certificate request, or CRL signature
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_sign
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *md"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_sign_ctx
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "EVP_MD_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_sign
.Fa "X509_REQ *x"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *md"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_sign_ctx
.Fa "X509_REQ *x"
.Fa "EVP_MD_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_CRL_sign
.Fa "X509_CRL *x"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *md"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_CRL_sign_ctx
.Fa "X509_CRL *x"
.Fa "EVP_MD_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_sign
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *md"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_sign_ctx
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "EVP_MD_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_sign
signs certificate
.Fa x
using private key
.Fa pkey
and message digest
.Fa md
and sets the signature in
.Fa x .
.Fn X509_sign_ctx
also signs certificate
.Fa x
but uses the parameters contained in digest context
.Fa ctx .
If the certificate information includes X.509 extensions, these two
functions make sure that the certificate bears X.509 version 3.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_sign ,
.Fn X509_REQ_sign_ctx ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_sign ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_sign_ctx ,
.Fn X509_CRL_sign ,
and
.Fn X509_CRL_sign_ctx
sign certificate requests and CRLs, respectively.
.Sh NOTES
.Fn X509_sign_ctx
is used where the default parameters for the corresponding public key
and digest are not suitable.
It can be used to sign keys using RSA-PSS for example.
.Pp
For efficiency reasons and to work around ASN.1 encoding issues the
encoding of the signed portion of a certificate, certificate request and
CRL is cached internally.
If the signed portion of the structure is modified the encoding is not
always updated meaning a stale version is sometimes used.
This is not normally a problem because modifying the signed portion will
invalidate the signature and signing will always update the encoding.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All functions return the size of the signature in bytes for success and
zero for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_add_entry_by_txt 3 ,
.Xr X509_new 3 ,
.Xr X509_verify_cert 3 ,
.Xr X509_verify 3 ,
.Xr X509_REQ_verify_ex 3 ,
.Xr X509_REQ_verify 3 ,
.Xr X509_CRL_verify 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn X509_sign ,
.Fn X509_REQ_sign
and
.Fn X509_CRL_sign
functions are available in all versions of OpenSSL.
.Pp
The
.Fn X509_sign_ctx ,
.Fn X509_REQ_sign_ctx
and
.Fn X509_CRL_sign_ctx
functions were added in OpenSSL 1.0.1.
.Pp
The
.Fn X509_ACERT_sign
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_sign_ctx
functions were added in OpenSSL 3.4.
